{soi} seems to have largely fallen out of use.

If you wanted to ask that question after someone has said {mi viska lo
nanmu}...

with soi, I think you could do {.i xu go'i soi do} which expands to {xu do
viska lo nanmu soi do} which I think does what you want.

Or you can just say {.i xu ji'a ny viska do}.  Also, while I love the
construct, I haven't seen a lot of vo'a and friends around.  I hope to see
them more though, they seem awfully useful.

Although, I'm not 100% sure what the difference is between {vo'a} and {lo
go'i}.

